; checklist: the three-layer object dialect of SPEC-019 (state rules).
;
; Layer 1, R5 shape + protocol: which acts exist and what may follow what.
; Layer 2, R6 roles (optional): who may send and receive each act.
; Layer 3, R7 state: how an accepted act moves each field of the instance.
;
; This is the checklist the cbcl-bus object SDK authors as a JSON contract
; (cbcl-bus SPEC-085 CON-001), written as one dialect. The name shown is
; illustrative; a deployed copy is named object-<dialect_hash of its body>
; (SPEC-019 R.6).
;
; `to` is the recipient set. The binder fills it from the accepted opener,
; or from the cast under R6, never from the caller (SPEC-019 R.5). What a
; consumer calls it, a room, a channel, a group, is the consumer's business.
;
; Nothing here declares `:replaces`. Installation adds `(require :replaces
; list)` to `check` and `drop` because the state clause names them as a
; register's writer and delete verb (SPEC-019 R.1, ADR-1901). The binder
; fills it; a caller may never set it; no rule reads it.
;
; Related specs:
;   specs/SPEC-019-state-rules.md   (R7 clause, binder, corpus)
;   specs/SPEC-002-structural-contracts.md (R5 protocol + shape grammar)
;   specs/SPEC-014-role-layer-endpoint-projection.md (R6 roles)

(define checklist (cbcl) @anuna
  (:resource-requirements
    ((max-depth 16)
     (max-expansion-size 4096)
     (verification-time 1000)))

  (:roles (owner (* member)))

  ; The opener: creates an instance in a fresh thread.
  (extend open (to title) :from owner :to (owner member)
    (tell to :title title))

  ; A write to the register keyed by :item.
  (extend check (to item done) :from member :to (owner member)
    (tell to :item item :done done))

  ; The register's delete verb: exactly the key.
  (extend drop (to item) :from owner :to (owner member)
    (tell to :item item))

  ; --- R5: shapes (closed by implication of the state clause) ---
  (shape open
    (require :title string))
  (shape check
    (require :item string)
    (require :done bool))
  (shape drop
    (require :item string))

  ; --- R5: causal protocol; repeatable acts each follow the opener ---
  (protocol
    (then begin open)
    (then open check)
    (then open drop))

  ; --- R7: state ---
  ; title: one value, greatest content address wins (uncontested).
  ; items: per :item key, one current :done value; a write is current
  ;        until a later write or drop of the same key names it in
  ;        :replaces; concurrent writes resolve by content address.
  (state
    (title (last open :title))
    (items (register-per-key check :item :done drop))))

; --- Worked trace (addresses abbreviated) ---
;
; Because the dialect declares roles, the thread's root is a with-roles
; wrapper carrying the cast (SPEC-014 CON-601), and every act's recipient
; set is its :to roles resolved through that cast (SPEC-019 R.5 step 3).
;
; M0  teach — the author distributes the dialect, R4-signed (R.6):
;   (meta (teach (define object-<hash> ...)))
;
; M0  root: the cast           by @aria; cast: owner=@aria, member={@bo @cy}
;   (with-roles ((owner @aria) (member @bo @cy)) :dialect sha256:<hash>
;     (signed @aria (hello :thread "list-1" :caused-by begin)))
;   The root is typed as `begin` (SPEC-014 REQ-623); the opener follows it.
;
; M1  root -> open             by @aria (owner)
;   (signed @aria (lang object-<hash> (open (@aria @bo @cy) :title "Launch tasks"
;     :caused-by sha256-<M0> :thread "list-1" :from @aria)))
;
; M2  open -> check            by @bo (member); no current write for "venue"
;   (signed @bo (lang object-<hash> (check (@aria @bo @cy) :item "venue" :done #f :replaces ()
;     :caused-by sha256-<M1> :thread "list-1" :from @bo)))
;
; M3  open -> check            by @bo; the binder fills :replaces (M2)
;   (signed @bo (lang object-<hash> (check (@aria @bo @cy) :item "venue" :done #t :replaces (sha256-<M2>)
;     :caused-by sha256-<M1> :thread "list-1" :from @bo)))
;
; M4  open -> drop             by @aria (owner); fills :replaces (M3)
;   (signed @aria (lang object-<hash> (drop (@aria @bo @cy) :item "venue" :replaces (sha256-<M3>)
;     :caused-by sha256-<M1> :thread "list-1" :from @aria)))
;
; A `drop` intent from @bo is rejected by the binder before signing: drop
; is :from owner and the cast binds owner to @aria alone (Role(owner)).
;
; State after {M0, M1, M2, M3}:  {"title": "Launch tasks", "items": {"venue": true}}
; State after {M0..M4}:           {"title": "Launch tasks", "items": {}}
; State after {M0, M1, M3, M4} (M2 not yet delivered): identical to the line
; above, and unchanged when M2 arrives (SPEC-019 R7).
